    {
        "id": "a4e8b1d7c0592f36",
        "type": "comment",
        "z": "7f3a1c9e2b4d5068",
        "name": "Read me before deploying",
        "info": "This example reads two tags from a WebIQ project.\n\nThe **WebIQ server** node is shipped **disabled** so that importing this\nflow cannot start connecting to anything by accident.\n\nTo run it:\n\n1. Open the **WebIQ server** node and fill in Host, Port, Project,\n   Username and Password for your own WebIQ runtime.\n2. Enable the node (right-click the node and choose Enable).\n3. Deploy, then press the inject button.\n\nThe node's status shows the connection state. `authenticated` (green)\nmeans it is ready to send commands. If it stays on\n`login timeout / project not found`, raise the **Login timeout** field;\nprojects backed by a slow PLC can need considerably longer than the\ndefault 5 seconds to answer a login.\n\nThe **API Request** node holds the full JSON payload sent to the server.\nEdit the `data` array to name the tags you want to read.",
        "x": 190,
        "y": 100,
        "wires": []
    },
    {
        "id": "c6d2f80a3e174b95",
        "type": "inject",
        "z": "7f3a1c9e2b4d5068",
        "name": "Trigger a read",
        "props": [
            {
                "p": "payload"
            }
        ],
        "repeat": "",
        "crontab": "",
        "once": false,
        "onceDelay": 0.1,
        "topic": "",
        "payload": "",
        "payloadType": "date",
        "x": 170,
        "y": 180,
        "wires": [
            [
                "e0b5947c1a8d2f63"
            ]
        ]
    },
